@startuml
' Stage 3 production-wiring pipeline: LanguageDef → in-Rho matching ruleset →
' capability-gated per-firing match call → matched + fired on the interpreter → OUT.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #37474F
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3E0
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #E65100
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F5F5F5
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9E9E9E
title Stage 3 — Production Wiring of In-Rho Set-Automaton Matching

|#DDE8FB|Compile-time — partial evaluation|
start
:LanguageDef;
:compile_in_rho_matching_ruleset;
note right
  Groups a language's structural base rewrites into
  ONE positional set automaton. Each accept channel is
  sourced from rho_net_injection_sites (the σ-receiver
  SOURCE — the triad anchor). TOTAL partition: every
  rewrite is an automaton entry OR a reasoned skip.
end note
:InRhoMatchingRuleset\n(automaton + accept_channels\n+ fingerprint + skip-list);

|#FCEBCF|Per-firing invocation — the F-stage|
:Dovetail report\n(the firing justification, host-matched);
if (every FIRED rule matchable in Rho?\nFV (ix) install_admits) then (no)
  :GATE REJECT — fall CLOSED to the\nhost-matched σ-replay driver\n(the language stays on its existing path);
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:reconstruct the ground subject LHS[σ]\n(root-rooted single redex; nested/multi\nfail closed → Stage 4);
:in_rho_match_call_par\n= receiver network  ‖  subject spread\n(single-shot, per-site nonce → O1);

|#D6EBDA|Runtime — the Rholang interpreter (RSpace)|
:installed σ-receivers  ‖  call;
:MATCH in Rho\n(the τ sa: symbol-inspection COMMs —\nunobservable, O1 symbol-once);
:FIRE the σ-receiver\n(one observable c(ℓ) COMM → ⟦R⟧σ);
:observe the rewrite result on OUT;
stop
@enduml
